Looking at this problem, I need to evaluate $I_n = \int_0^\infty \left(\operatorname{E}_n(x)e^x - \frac{1}{1+x}\right) dx$ and show it equals $-\psi(n)$.

**Answer leak check:** The problem asks to "show that it equals $-\psi(n)$" — this is the statement to prove, not a leaked solution. No solution sketch or proof is embedded. Proceeding.

